WEBVTT

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:02.730
I'm bringing this Kishin down!

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:06.720
That miner brat is at it again?!

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:08.590
You're wasting your time!

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:10.750
The mighty Kishin's flames shall turn you to ash!

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.620
I can't jump in headfirst like Musashi...

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:19.710
Dammit.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:34.300
Damn! No matter where I cut,
 it just grows back!

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:36.140
What the—

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:37.720
Musashi!

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.050
What's the big idea?!

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.570
This is our camp.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.520
<i>We'll make sure to take care of it for you.</i>

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:56.420
You...

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:00.810
Let me go! Why are you trying to stop me?

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.270
That thing is gonna be my first prize!

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:06.480
Your first prize, huh?

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:08.740
To what end, exactly?

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:10.640
It's for my dream!

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.220
Isn't that the kinda thing 
you risk your life for?

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:16.470
Your dream? Hmm...

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:20.670
Sounds like you're taking this a 
bit lightly to be gambling your life.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:22.210
We're a band of Bushi.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:25.530
We can't let some reckless kid
 run out onto the battlefield.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:26.690
I'm not reckless!

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:29.890
You sure about that?! Kishin 
regenerate from superficial damage!

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:32.020
How were you planning to kill one by yourself?!

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:33.980
Look!

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:35.360
<i>This</i> is your foe.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.360
Restraint unit is in position!

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.440
Keep the Kishin's legs bound!

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:40.780
It takes a whole band of Bushi 
working together to fight one.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:45.210
You can go after it on your own, 
but you'll never take it down!

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:50.060
You haven't fought or thought enough 
to go around talking about big dreams!

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:52.050
Give up on hunting this Kishin!

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:28.930
<b>The Outside World</b>

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:38.840
Maybe he's right... That thing is huge.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:40.930
There's no way I can beat it alone...

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:43.650
But even so!

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.210
What's with him?

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:45.910
Whoa there!

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:47.220
I have to go.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:49.720
If you try to break free, 
you'll just hurt yourself!

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:53.450
I don't know why...

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.620
But if I don't,
 I'll regret it till the day I die.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.410
Hey, he's getting away!

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:05.830
You wanna grab him again, Captain?

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:07.920
It's all right.

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:10.900
He's definitely determined.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:15.720
If the kid's got something he's 
willing to risk his life for...

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:17.550
then he really is a Bushi.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:23.990
I...

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:27.740
What exactly can I do?

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:33.160
Crane Wings in the Blue Sky, 
targeting the enemy core.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:39.360
Twelve seconds until firing. Eleven... Ten...

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:42.640
This is bad! They're aiming for the core horn!

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:43.890
Core horn?

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.830
Hey, hang on! What's a core horn?!

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:50.710
Musashi's risking his life! 
I'm not just gonna turn tail and run!

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:55.080
Don't do it, Red!

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:57.490
You're headed right into our attack!

00:04:57.490 --> 00:04:58.090
Beat it!

00:04:58.380 --> 00:04:59.540
<i>Not a chance.</i>

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:03.190
<i>I'm done letting people
 keep me from what I want.</i>

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:05.780
<i>I'm never doing that again!</i>

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:16.130
This here should do it.

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:23.340
Repeatedly strike the same point

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:26.410
to breach a hole that will sink any foe!

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:42.820
Crane Wings in the Blue Sky in...

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:45.120
Five. Four. Three.

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:48.320
Kanemaki-Isshin Style 
demolition technique...

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:49.820
Greatsword Slayer!

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:04.880
Hold your positions!

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.590
If the Kishin gets loose...

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:09.100
Crane Wings in the Blue Sky, fire!

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:15.690
Crane Wings in the Blue Sky missed!

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:28.190
Before they can finish things off, I will!

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:31.540
I'll put an end to this!

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:39.130
<i>You can go after it on your own, 
but you'll never take it down!</i>

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:41.930
I gotta do what I can!

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:43.970
Musashi! Go for the thing 
on the Kishin's navel!

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:46.760
That's its core horn—its weakness!

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:49.410
Smash the horn on its navel 
and it's dead meat!

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:50.770
Kojiro?

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:56.550
You always run off half-cocked. 
You need somebody watching your back.

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:58.520
Thanks, Kojiro!

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:01.470
So that's the Kishin's weakness?!

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:08.430
Engoku Tengu the red Kishin...

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:11.380
is mine to defeat!

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:20.030
He did it!

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:30.210
My katana...!

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:32.260
Musashi, look out! In front of you!

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:38.630
Dammit...

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:42.980
You've proven how serious you are, 
but I'll take it from here.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:43.820
What?!

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:57.640
The captain finished it off!

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:00.920
Sorry, kid!

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:04.760
I'm afraid I had to steal your big first step.

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:08.580
Dammit! Kojiro and I were 
supposed to beat that thing!

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:12.960
That's too bad. But we're
 fighting for our own reasons.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:18.930
Look alive. The Kishin's body 
is about to fall apart.

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:37.030
The mighty Kishin has fallen!

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:38.420
Awesome...

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:47.800
What are you doing?

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:50.760
Absorbing the Kishin's power.

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:57.440
Raise your voices in celebration!

00:08:57.440 --> 00:09:01.640
Engoku Tengu the red Kishin
has been slain by the Takeda Band!

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:07.180
Dammit...

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:09.100
I guess they beat us.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:10.710
Kojiro?

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:15.630
Our first prize... Losing it like this 
is actually pretty frustrating.

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:16.570
Yeah...

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:21.080
Hey, is it me, or is this sight familiar?

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:28.040
<i>It's just like the art on that 
scroll about Bushi bands!</i>

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:32.040
Thank you! You're a hero! 
You've saved our city!

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:33.440
The only force able to stand up to the oni...

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:34.030
If you hadn't shown up,

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:36.570
Bushi really aren't villains after all.

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:36.970
we would've been slaves to the oni 
for the rest of our lives!

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:41.250
Everything Dad told me... It was all true.

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:46.980
I'm happy for you, Kojiro.

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:56.530
I'm Takeda Naotora of the Takeda Band,
 and you have my word...

00:09:56.530 --> 00:10:00.480
We'll slay all of the Kishin and 
make the world safe for mankind again!

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:04.490
How many people before you have
 spouted that exact nonsense?!

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:06.230
It's been 150 years!

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:09.200
The mighty Kishin have multiplied 
and grown in power!

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:12.980
Meanwhile, you Bushi bands continue 
your pointless resistance

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:17.320
with no thought for the innocent civilians
 caught up in your conflicts!

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:20.010
Are you going to drag everyone
into the depths of despair again

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:25.620
for the sake of some impossible 
dream, Takeda Naotora?!

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:29.440
An impossible dream, huh?

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:33.730
I grew up hearing that over and over.

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:37.170
It's not like every Bushi among 
the bands agrees either.

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:40.320
Some think stability should take 
priority over eliminating the oni.

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:42.940
Some want a future with no oni at all.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:45.320
But the thing we all have in common

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:48.610
is that the oni force us to base our 
lives and dreams around them.

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:51.760
So we dream impossible dreams

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:54.800
before having to give up,
 passing it all on to those who come after.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:57.100
We inherit wishes,

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:59.520
as well as the names 
and techniques of our forbears.

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:04.350
The strength of the dead comrades 
passes from their swords to ours,

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:08.960
and in our hands now, 
 they're stronger than ever before!

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:15.000
To look up and behold 
the blue sky without fear...

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:20.160
Isn't that what you want for your children?

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:26.060
I mean to put an end to this.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.770
Our generation will finally be victorious.

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:36.040
We'll make a world free of the monsters 
that came to this land 150 years ago!

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:40.500
I'll continue to fight for the 
sake of my comrades and my clan.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:43.020
And I ask that you all 
lend us your strength.

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:45.430
Freedom for Hinomoto!

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:52.100
He's just like the Bushi that my dad used 
to talk about! Don't you think, Musashi?

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.730
<i>I can't stand this!</i>

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:07.980
<i>He stole my glory!</i>

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:13.310
He's looking this way!

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:16.050
I'm done lying about how I really feel...

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:17.950
I'm gonna let him have it!

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:21.510
Uh, hi! I'm Kanemaki Kojiro, and this is Musashi.

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:26.220
Kojiro and Musashi, huh? 
I feel bad about taking your first prize.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:30.000
It's okay! We just weren't strong enough.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.920
We're not really in any position to complain.

00:12:32.220 --> 00:12:36.890
That's right, Red! 
The captain saved your life.

00:12:36.890 --> 00:12:38.870
Can't complain about that, can you?

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:42.170
The oni are our real enemy.

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:45.420
Only third-rate Bushi fight other Bushi.

00:12:47.770 --> 00:12:49.730
<i>Maybe they're right.</i>

00:12:49.730 --> 00:12:51.860
<i>Everyone's so happy.</i>

00:12:52.570 --> 00:12:57.080
<i>Maybe I should just... 
keep a lid on how I feel.</i>

00:12:58.740 --> 00:12:59.550
Musashi.

00:13:00.660 --> 00:13:02.830
You've got a lot of potential, kid.

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:08.210
You're weak now, but keep working hard. 
Maybe you'll catch up to me one day!

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:12.480
Hey, the captain gave you his approval!

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:13.970
Good for you, Red!

00:13:13.970 --> 00:13:16.300
<i>Don't say it... Don't say it...</i>

00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:20.020
He saved your hide, y'know! 
The least you could do is thank him.

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:21.730
He's right, Musashi.

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:23.310
Shut it!

00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:26.810
Quit acting so high and mighty, 
you kill-stealing samurai!

00:13:26.810 --> 00:13:30.040
Hey! Show the captain some 
respect, you little brat!

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:31.310
Shut up!

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:32.460
What was that?!

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:36.000
I swore I'd never just 
go with the flow again, so listen up!

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:40.520
I'm super pissed we lost our first prize!

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:44.980
Aw, the little redhead is such a weirdo!

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:45.620
Yeah, that's something all right.

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:47.330
Sure is.

00:13:47.330 --> 00:13:52.390
You weren't sure whether or not to complain 
out of consideration for those around you.

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:56.360
It took guts to come clean, didn't it?

00:13:58.030 --> 00:14:01.090
I like people with guts.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:06.750
You can have this, Musashi.

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:10.390
I'm Takeda Naotora.

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:14.090
What is this thing, Naotora?

00:14:21.010 --> 00:14:25.220
Your "sucks that you didn't get
 to kill a Kishin" consolation prize!

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:33.680
You'll have to find the next one yourself.

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:35.650
That should come in handy.

00:14:35.650 --> 00:14:36.850
See ya!

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:39.680
Hey, what exactly is that, Musashi?

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:42.950
Musashi?

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:48.820
This sucks!

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:53.330
This sucks... This sucks so bad...

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:57.530
What's your problem? 
Naotora seems nice enough.

00:14:57.530 --> 00:14:59.220
How do you figure?!

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:02.000
Didn't you see what a jerk he was being?
Don't be fooled, Kojiro!

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:06.980
That nasty gloryhog! 
Are you even listening, Kojiro?!

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:11.550
Hey, that's the Aki Province seal, which means...

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:13.850
This belongs to an official!

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:15.470
What kind of a reward is this?!

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:16.060
Hey, don't!

00:15:16.980 --> 00:15:18.010
It's...

00:15:18.380 --> 00:15:19.790
a kaleidoscope!

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:22.120
A kaleidoscope?

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:24.810
I think so! It's really sparkly.

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:29.500
Why would an official have a toy, though?

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:34.560
Huh... I feel like I've seen 
this somewhere before.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:36.990
Yeah? Where?

00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:39.840
I know!

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:45.580
The Bushi scrolls, huh?

00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:47.480
I haven't seen this in a while.

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:48.200
Right here!

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:51.170
See? It looks like he's using that thing.

00:15:52.030 --> 00:15:54.320
I can sorta see the resemblance...

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:54.990
Huh?

00:15:54.990 --> 00:15:55.950
What is it?

00:15:55.950 --> 00:16:00.660
That pattern on the scroll... 
It's the same as inside the kaleidoscope.

00:16:00.660 --> 00:16:01.870
Really?

00:16:01.870 --> 00:16:04.650
But this isn't a pattern. It's an oni.

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:05.780
It's an oni?

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:08.620
I get it!

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:13.520
This is a tool that lets you see oni!

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:15.830
A tool that let's you see oni?

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:16.670
Yeah!

00:16:16.670 --> 00:16:18.900
Remember what Naotora said?

00:16:18.900 --> 00:16:20.950
We'll have to find our next Kishin ourselves!

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:23.720
And this is gonna help us do it!

00:16:23.720 --> 00:16:27.720
He might've taken our first prize, 
but now we can make up the lost ground.

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:29.580
Just you wait, Naotora!

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:32.200
Maybe this is something, too...

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:36.340
Like those flying, glowing katanas 
that the Takeda Band was using.

00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:40.430
It might be! Maybe if we keep reading,
 we can find out a bunch more.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:42.580
This is...

00:16:43.620 --> 00:16:44.850
impossible to read!

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:46.920
Can you take it from here, ace student?

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:47.770
You bet!

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:52.820
Let's see here.
"Hinomoto was once a human land...

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:59.010
But with the sudden appearance of the 
enigmatic oni, their rule came to an end.

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:03.620
The famous Warring States generals 
fell one after another,

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:09.910
but the domination of oni must be resisted. 
The Kishin in Hinomoto now...

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:11.580
number upward of a hundred."

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:11.920
<b>Upward of a Hundred</b>

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:14.130
There're that many?

00:17:14.570 --> 00:17:16.450
Hey, Kojiro, look!

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:19.350
It's the names of different Kishin!

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:21.640
See? Engoku Tengu is here!

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:25.500
There're so many... Just look at all of 'em!

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:28.210
Well, we'll have plenty of chances 
to make up for this time.

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:29.830
You bet we will!

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:32.530
"To the samurai who would defy the oni,

00:17:33.470 --> 00:17:37.160
Kishin are supernatural beings that come 
in a multitude of shapes and sizes.

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:40.020
Their power is like that of the gods.

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:44.940
But if these gods seek to crush 
man under their feet,

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:49.470
then let them all be slain so that 
humanity may retake the world."

00:17:51.490 --> 00:17:55.500
<i>It is a dream that has yet 
to be fulfilled by anyone.</i>

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:58.930
<i>It is the one true duty of the Bushi.</i>

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:01.690
A dream so big no one 
has been able to achieve it!

00:18:01.690 --> 00:18:03.160
A Bushi's duty...

00:18:03.730 --> 00:18:05.270
<i>Samurai of the land,</i>

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:08.830
<i>let your ambitions contend with one 
another as you seek to fell the Kishin.</i>

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:14.030
<i>When the deed is done, 
the fractured nation will be healed.</i>

00:18:14.670 --> 00:18:19.790
<i>The divine treasures will return to the hands
 of the top Bushi who slay the top Kishin.</i>

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:23.360
<i>And when that happens, 
the land will be unified.</i>

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:23.700
<b>Unified Land</b>

00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:25.280
The land will be unified?!

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:29.930
<i>And the one responsible 
for this new union, the Great Unifier,</i>

00:18:29.930 --> 00:18:33.210
<i>will reign as the new king of Hinomoto!</i>

00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:36.390
The Great Unifier will unite the country!

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:38.580
They never mentioned this in school...

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:41.450
Yeah, but the Takeda Band knew about it.

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:43.720
Remember what he said?

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:46.230
They have their own reasons for fighting.

00:18:47.260 --> 00:18:49.970
Hey, Musashi! Where are you going?

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:56.200
<i>After everyone else in this country cast aside
their pride and gave up resisting the oni,</i>

00:18:56.820 --> 00:19:01.920
<i>the Bushi continued to fight 
for humanity's place in the world.</i>

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:04.810
<i>That is their way of life.</i>

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:07.340
You wanna unite the country, right?!

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:14.050
That's what you're fighting for!

00:19:14.050 --> 00:19:16.040
I'm impressed you figured it out, Musashi.

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:20.270
Every last Kishin in Hinomoto needs to go.
 And we're going to make it happen!

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:24.770
Fighting those things isn't some game.
 You won't be able to do it.

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:29.260
Yeah, well, you guys haven't 
managed it yet either, have you?

00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:32.000
This kid...

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:33.520
He's pretty bold!

00:19:33.830 --> 00:19:35.570
It's been 150 years.

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:38.900
This dream is so big that 
no one's been able to accomplish it!

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:42.900
And if no one else is up to the task,
then I'm gonna do it!

00:19:42.900 --> 00:19:47.510
I don't care how strong these monsters are!
 I'm gonna take down all of the Kishin!

00:19:47.510 --> 00:19:50.000
That'll unify the country, right?!

00:19:51.410 --> 00:19:52.820
Go ahead and try!

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:19.470
I wonder what the world 
is like outside of town.

00:20:19.470 --> 00:20:22.000
No one's gonna be around 
to help us next time.

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:23.690
I still wanna go.

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:27.650
Because... this is what I've wanted 
to do all this time!

00:20:27.650 --> 00:20:30.310
Musashi! Kojiro!

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:32.350
Be safe!

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:34.340
Good luck fighting the oni!

00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:36.800
Yeah! We're heading out now!

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:55.090
It's huge! So this is what it's like...

00:20:55.090 --> 00:20:58.890
Look! Tatsuyama is downright tiny from here.

00:20:58.890 --> 00:21:02.640
We spent our whole lives 
in that little place.

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:07.890
If you and your dad hadn't 
taught me swordsmanship,

00:21:07.890 --> 00:21:12.390
I would probably still be digging up rocks 
with nothing to dream of.

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:13.930
Musashi...

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:21.920
Thinking about it now, I'm really 
glad that I met the two of you.

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:25.120
I see.

00:23:25.350 --> 00:23:26.980
A flying fortress!

00:23:26.980 --> 00:23:28.660
I wonder how it works.

00:23:28.660 --> 00:23:31.020
You're wondering how 
the flying fortress works?

00:23:31.020 --> 00:23:33.970
You ride a Kitetsu Mount and you don't know?

00:23:34.290 --> 00:23:37.420
Hey, yeah, Kojiro! 
How's this thing run, anyway?

00:23:37.420 --> 00:23:40.030
No clue. We'll probably find 
out soon enough, though.

00:23:37.640 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Next Time
The Kosameda Band</b>
